749:+- **Same-boot journal window since anchor** — explicit read-only probe `tools/mori-journal-window.py --anchor PATH --scope user|system` (round-16 build; admitted round 16 — `corpus/lessons/round-16-verifier-spotcheck.md:11`). Reads one journal scope from an operator-retained `mori-journal-anchor-v1` cursor using MESSAGE-free output fields. The first record must match the anchor cursor and boot exactly and is dropped; every later record must be a scalar-cursor object in that same boot. Reports `records_after_anchor` and four separate `positive_*` subset counts (kernel OOM, unit OOM, unit signal, process SIGKILL) using the r15 predicates; no total, victim, emitter or completeness claim. Missing or vacuumed anchor, boot mismatch, malformed, duplicate or truncated capture, nonzero rc, stderr, timeout and overflow return `MORI_JOURNAL_WINDOW_UNAVAILABLE` with no positive totals. Byte equality is conservative: libsystemd documents that one entry may carry several cursor strings, so a mismatch refuses without proving deletion and no dedup is claimed. The anchor is never advanced, stored or written by the probe.
