• Now I have substantial material. Key findings:

  1. **The moving-target problem is real and material.** The assigned tripwire `git diff master -- . ':!.ufo/waves/round-43/w1'` found 5 prose matches at T2, then found NOTHING at T3 because commit dde525ea landed mid-attack. The committed content (171 files, 30k lines, including `count-c1s.py` 172 lines, `count-c2.py` 91 lines, `mori-disk-rate.py` 300 lines, and `.ufo/waves/round-43/assimilation/...` stuff) is invisible to the assigned command post-commit. This is the strongest counterexample to the scope bound as-a-command: **the bound is time-of-day sensitive and after the round commits, `diff master` is a no-op that can never FAIL anything.**

